 @urnamed32  Depends on use case and build but for am4 and gaming a 6700xt in most markets new is 279, so that or a 2nd hand 6800/6950xt (300-550) depending on budget and use as the 16gbs vram is great, but for streaming and graphic design ngreedia is the way though so probably a 2nd hand 2080ti for 200+ or if that 3070 was somehow around 299 it could be alright for a little bit (eg maybe 2 years at 1080p+ depending on games etc) but note that 8gbs esp for modern releases isn't enough for 1080p native, with high settings, even without RT in certain cases eg jedi surivior and tlou etc, so if you're fine missing the odd game and can wait for patches (3-6months usually) as well as dont mind playing non rt high settings 8gbs should suffice but16gbs is enough to run most games in max 4k (with 12gbs pushing it on 1440p with rt in some of said modern releases but minus rt and said modern dud it's also smooth as butter there) so if you intend to have said gpu for over 2+ years eg 3-5+ I would implore you to get something with at least 10-12gbs of vram and preferably 16gbs+ to be safe (as the 6800 2nd hand is a banger at 300-350, as is the newly lowered msrp 6950xt on bundles from 550-600 etc) but it all comes down to avaiability and price eg region etc, full build and so on.

Obligitory ARC mention: If it's a creator rig and it's both not your main rig or first tiem troubleshooting pcs etc (as it's still first gen) then the A770 16gb at 250-300 is a great deal as it's competing with the 3070 regularly esp at 1440p, has AV1 encoding, looks sleek af and has lots of growth as it's driver support has the most potencial improvements as well as longevity in terms of being supported(as is the A750 at 199 and below as it trades blows with the 3060 for half the price and still has Av1 support etc, as does the 6600xt etc at that price point esp with the 7600 etc right around the corner prices are about to plummet) so technically wait for battlemage but if you need something now for 1080p a 1080ti would even do still as would a 5700xt oc (they can still smash 1440p+) etc

tldr: 1080ti/5700xt (oc)/2080ti/6700xt/6800/6950xt or if you know how to troubleshoot/need AV1 and it's not your main rig ARC A750/A770 16gb

