 @sweetsurrender815  The performance uplift over the 3060Ti is negligible except in ray tracing and it doesn't have enough VRAM for some games that were out before its release, which isn't helped by the gimped memory interface. It can also only use 8 PCIE lanes, a direct downgrade that shouldn't reduce performance on a PCIE gen 4 system, but could be worse in a PCIE gen 3 systems like those running B350 boards.  
The only actual advantages over the 2.5 year old card this thing replaces are in ray tracing and support for DLSS with frame gen, while in other respects it is either the same or worse while still being named a 60Ti and having the same launch MSRP the 3060Ti did. 

Even if it was slightly cheaper than the 3060Ti is currently priced it would be a joke. Just barely not a generational downgrade overall.

